{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology","id":144922,"title":"Unified Cosmology","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-21T15:12:03-07:00","id":144922,"title":"Unified Cosmology","content":"Yeah, I know the WoD is modular, and each person's WoD includes as much or as little as wanted. In spite of that, I'm curious if anyone has come up with a Grand Unified Theory of the World of Darkness. There are a few (very cool) pictures out there that illustrate ideas of the relationships between the visible world and everything else, but I'm sure the arrival of the God Machine messed that up.<br /> <br /> Anyways, anyone with tons of spare time (something I don't have) work this out?<br /> <br /> EDIT: The purpose of this thread is not to write &quot;sorry, WoD can't be done that way&quot;. It can, just not in an official capacity, which is good. So, if you have come up with your own unified cosmology, I am curious to hear it because of reasons. I like the mystery and whatnot, and in the course of running a game have never really had cosmology come up, but am still curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","user":"ChewyGranola","date":". 05-21-2014, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T15:23:29-07:00","id":144931,"title":"","content":"It's not really possible to do. The authors have come out and stated that there are intentionally contradictory sections of the lore between splats, representing their particular small and isolated perspectives on a literally universal problem. <br /> <br /> Even without that though, part of the point of WoD is horror and mystery, I don't see what's to be gained from anyone knowing exactly what's going on other than individual storytellers. It seems to me that sort of thing would practically be begging for a rules-lawyering player to come along and start bickering with the ST about how this or that can't happen because the cosmology says this. <br /> <br /> Really just a matter of preference, admittedly I prefer it to be intentionally impossible and paradoxical because that's the way I see the universe being anyway. If you like neatly layered planes and a, shall we say, mechanistic *wink*wink*nudge*nudge* order to things, then you are free to create one for yourself and your games. <br /> <br /> On the matter of the GMC specifically, that's also left intentionally vague. The way I've read it, it primarily occupies the Material, both in solid and twilight forms, with occasional infrastructure in the Shadow and Hedge. Oh... and it occupies different timelines as well. That'll make mapping it effectively impossible right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","user":"Anachronistic Jam","date":". 05-21-2014, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T15:47:26-07:00","id":144978,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the WoD can be 'mapped' in the way a lot of illustrators try. I imagine the best way of expressing the underlying metaphysics is as a multi-axial spectrum that represents contrasting 'states of being; rather than strictly being locational","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T16:03:06-07:00","id":144991,"title":"","content":"As I said, I am well aware that the WoD can't be &quot;mapped&quot; and there's horror and mystery contradictions and all that. BUT, if anyone has THEIR OWN ideas about a unified cosmology, I would love to read them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T16:11:21-07:00","id":144995,"title":"","content":"Mine's incredibly general and still requires multiple layers to get around the limitations of two-dimensional cartography, but the core gist of it, expressed as linearly as convenient, is thus:<br /> <br /> Limiting the graphed portions to the level of accessibility conventionally thought of as material\u2026<br /> Earth* ** (+ various frequencies of Twilight) | [Loci/Verges] (Gauntlet) | Shadow* | ???<br /> * | [Hedge Gates] | The Hedge*** | [Trods] (Wall Before Arcadia) | Arcadia | ???<br /> * | [Avernian Gates]*** (Impenetrable Darkness) | Autochthonous Depths*** | [Ferrymen] (Rivers) | Lower Mysteries*** | ???<br /> <br /> ??? = Strangeness Of Varying Provenance (Lower Depths [including Abaddon], Abyss, Astral, Supernal, Other Unsorted; particulars depend on context and are heavily speculative.)<br /> (element) = Liminal space/barrier not typically large enough to be explored as a whole place unto itself divorced from the context of its bordering territories<br /> [element] = Means of transition<br /> *, **, ***, etc = Connections more complex than can be graphed in this format, e.g. vertical, shortcutting, etc<br /> <br /> Earth's sundry flavors of Twilight contain, besides denizens and objects, some quantity of extra space - it's where a few of the God-Machine's facilities are packed up in, if I remember correctly - and many otherworlds have a sort of fourth directional axis that can be described as &quot;toward/away from Earthly human experience&quot; - the Underworld, for instance, manifests this direction in the form of the constant slope, and the Hedge doubles it up as the direction of &quot;toward Arcadia.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sympathetic resonance is important for just about every extramundane denizen, perhaps best exemplified by the fact that banishing all traces of a thing from an area is the general means of summoning a creature that eats or corrupts that thing, but weird distant confluences can secure more temporary and less conditional visits while (to borrow a phrase) the stars are right. Ghosts in particular have trouble managing the maintenance of that resonance while retaining the things that make them passably human in a place that mostly lacks them in the flavors that they most need - memory is their big Essence stipend early on for just that reason.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, supernatural locales tend to bleed into their visitors - even something as relatively innocuous as the Astral can have physical effects past the Temenos and has &quot;naturalized&quot; one of the Fae enough that it operates off of the same mechanics as the natives, to say nothing of the risks Sin-Eaters take by spending too long in the Underworld or the tidbits Werewolf mentions about how extended stays in the Shadow can warp a being. It's entirely probable that some of the stranger denizens of those locales wandered in from elsewhere and got shuffled into the thematics of the place - &quot;as above, so below&quot; shows this even extends to the Supernal, as could be expected for a place that describes other places in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Changeling's take on the various otherworlds is sort of a metaphysical blob - the Skein doesn't differentiate overmuch between types of dreamers, and Arcadia is basically interchangeable with any of the stuff I tossed into the ??? stack; the Hedge does likewise with any of the intermediary realms to some degree.<br /> <br /> The Astral, the Supernal, and the Abyss cosmologically exist in a kind of veneer over everything, conceptual realms as they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-21-2014, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T23:41:04-07:00","id":145345,"title":"","content":"I've been told I need the Astral, but I'd have to redo the map, since I forgot to save the base (it's kind of <i>huge</i>).<br /> <br /> But here's the first draft of the <i>Planeswalker's Guide to the World of Darkness</i>. I plan on maybe one day if I'm not lazy making a better map and creating a document to go along with it (possibly written in character as Lark Demonde) describing how the various playable characters react inside various &quot;Occult Realms&quot;. Like, I feel that Prometheans could recover Pyros inside an Infrastructure facility as well as a Demon could, but that their flux tears apart the Infrastructure faster (basically, extra quick Wasteland) because I like the idea that the Principle and the God-Machine are connected somehow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/Q2cWo6f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/Q2cWo6f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/Q2cWo6f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i.imgur.com/Q2cWo6f.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":".  I couldn't get the picture to upload 05-22-2014, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T03:35:50-07:00","id":145499,"title":"","content":"I'd try to be careful about trying to explain everything from Mage cosmology. Some fans have a tendency to do that. However, the Astral, the Supernal Realms etc. do not appear in <i>any</i> other game but Mage. The only justification for inflating their importance is to better support the themes of Mage where you're supposed to be involved with some ultimate secrets of reality. But it should never be used as an excuse to lord Mages over other characters. A Mage would be no more capable of entering the Underworld or Arcadia than a Changeling or Geist would be capable of travelling to the Astral &amp; Supernal.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Supernal Realms almost always get a major part even tho Mages can't even really visit there; the true Mage &quot;domain&quot; is the Astral. What's up with that, eh?)<br /> <br /> Generally most supernaturals have their own realms, like:<br /> <br /> Mage: Astral -&gt; Supernal<br /> Chengeling: Hedge -&gt; Arcadia<br /> Werewolf: Shadow -&gt; Penumbra<br /> etc.<br /> <br /> Usually the 1st realm (which can be travelled and is visited by the PCs frequently) is supported by a &quot;deeper&quot; realm where some sort of essence or truth can be found and which is difficult to reach. Of course, the nature of these depends on the splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=145345#post145345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been told I need the Astral, but I'd have to redo the map, since I forgot to save the base (it's kind of <i>huge</i>).<br /> <br /> But here's the first draft of the <i>Planeswalker's Guide to the World of Darkness</i>. I plan on maybe one day if I'm not lazy making a better map and creating a document to go along with it (possibly written in character as Lark Demonde) describing how the various playable characters react inside various &quot;Occult Realms&quot;. Like, I feel that Prometheans could recover Pyros inside an Infrastructure facility as well as a Demon could, but that their flux tears apart the Infrastructure faster (basically, extra quick Wasteland) because I like the idea that the Principle and the God-Machine are connected somehow.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/Q2cWo6f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.imgur.com/Q2cWo6f.jpg</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> It's the Mummy and Geist cosmology that's different to reconcile in a crossover since they have two separate underworlds. Even if you could perhaps like, make the Mummy underworld an unique place carved into the Geist underworld, they are different thematically.<br /> <br /> These &quot;lower&quot; realms are also interesting. &quot;Inferno&quot; on says this much about Hell: once you have fallen into a portal to hell, there's no way out. &quot;There's a reason&quot; it says &quot;that it's called 'damnation'.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T04:51:59-07:00","id":145527,"title":"","content":"Mages <i>can</i> go to the Underworld. Quite easily, actually - Moros can sense Avernian Gates with Mage Sight, and pop them open with starting-level spells. Masters can make their own gates to anywhere in the Underworld they want to go, or summon ghosts back from the Underworld into Twilight.<br /> <br /> The main disadvantages mages have in the Underworld are;<br /> <br /> a) their Virtue and Vice get swapped like everyone else<br /> b) they're alive, and very obviously not natives<br /> c) they have no inbuilt ability to cross Rivers like Sin-Eaters do<br /> <br /> But all of those can be alleviated by magic for the determined cosmological spelunker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T05:32:29-07:00","id":145574,"title":"","content":"^guess I lied then<br /> sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T05:36:46-07:00","id":145579,"title":"","content":"The only unifying cosmology I have is that everything, <i>everything</i>, is true and trying to kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T08:20:15-07:00","id":145675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=145579#post145579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only unifying cosmology I have is that everything, <i>everything</i>, is true and trying to kill you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my favorite answer so far. Nice one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T08:34:13-07:00","id":145681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=145675#post145675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my favorite answer so far. Nice one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Damnit son you should've said I wouldn't have typed so many words","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T09:26:20-07:00","id":145740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=145681#post145681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damnit son you should've said I wouldn't have typed so many words</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey I liked yours too! No hate! I just enjoyed the simple, to the point nature of Flyboys, that's all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T13:18:57-07:00","id":145967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=145579#post145579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only unifying cosmology I have is that everything, <i>everything</i>, is true and trying to kill you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would slightly rephrase to, &quot;It doesn't matter what's true, so don't bother, everything out there either doesn't care about you or considers you food. Act accordingly.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T13:20:19-07:00","id":145969,"title":"","content":"If I were going to map out the nWoD, I'd leave a lot of uncertainty and ambiguity in the cosmological model I went with. It wouldn't feel right, otherwise.<br /> <br /> As an example:<br /> <br /> There's the Supernal, and maybe the Empyrean &quot;above&quot; it. The Supernal is pure symbolism, the abstract forms and archetypes that give rise to reality as we know it. Whether there's a Divine Fire burning above it, shining through into reality below like the sun through a stained-glass window...who knows? Who <i>can</i> know?<br /> <br /> The Abyss is the lies and distortion that twist the expression of Supernal symbols in the phenomenal world. It didn't exist before humans bodily entered the Supernal and started messing around with the symbols they found there, creating contradictions and paradoxes; the Abyss is, effectively, one big Aponoia. Or possibly the sum total of every Aponoia ever inflicted upon existence.<br /> <br /> The Astral Realms (specifically, the Dreamtime) used to bridge into the Supernal. Now the Abyss cuts off the path. Even before the Abyss, though, mages didn't travel bodily to the Supernal. The process of astrally travelling there naturally imposed the accumulated context and imagery of the mage's dream-journey along the Astral Path up to that point upon the Supernal--sort of like a Lustrum, except that since the mage wasn't entirely &quot;there&quot; in the Supernal, they were neither at risk of being erased if the &quot;Lustrum&quot; failed (they'd just wake up) nor able to influence or alter the symbols they encountered. They were unable, in other words, to perform acts of Imperium.<br /> <br /> The Emanation Realms are sort of...in between symbolic and literal reality. Some verges open up not into the Shadow but into an Emanation Realm. Some &quot;places-that-aren't&quot; in the Shadow are, or contain, gateways into resonant Emanation Realms. Really, Emanation Realms may overlap with any place in the World of Darkness. It may be that the Celestial Ladder went through, or was, an Emanation Realm. (Or it could simply have been a fancy name for a magical working that made it possible for mages to become archmasters.)<br /> <br /> Twilight isn't a realm so much as a state of being for ephemeral entities: the state of being present in the material world but unable to interact with it.<br /> <br /> The Shadow lies &quot;across&quot; the Gauntlet, overlapping the material world. Wounds may simply be areas of highly malignant Essence, or they may be rips in the &quot;fabric&quot; of the Shadow leading to other realms. Places-that-aren't, likewise, may be, or contain, or overlap with, other realms, though this is far from universal.<br /> <br /> The Underworld lies past the Avernian Gates, &quot;beneath&quot; the material world. Some of the Lower Mysteries may be, or contain, or overlap with, other realms--most likely Stygian Emanation Realms or the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is the gateway/barrier between Arcadia and Earth. This may or may not be the same Arcadia as the Supernal Realm described in Mage. The Hedge may or may not be an Emanation Realm of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine exists in, and is intertwined with, the material world. Its angels may be deliberately constructed as ephemeral entities native to the material world, or they may be summoned from somewhere else. Or both. Or something stranger.<br /> <br /> The Principle may likewise exist within and intertwined with the material world. Or it may exist somewhere else, sending its qashmallim to act as its eyes, ears, and hands in this reality.<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths aren't one realm so much as they are a label for particularly weird and sinister realities with no apparent connection to &quot;known&quot; cosmology. They are the &quot;Here Be Dragons&quot; at the edge of the map. If there's any unifying characteristic at all, it's that each of them seems to be a place where at least one of the Arcana...isn't. Not twisted in its expression, as with the Abyss, but simply <i>not there</i>. (Even this may be only a trait held in common by a particular set of Lower Depths realms; the whole point is that the Lower Depths are unknown and quite possibly unknowable.) Potential Lower Depths realms include the Inferno (which may or may not be the same place as Abaddon as described in Imperial Mysteries), whatever shadowy world the Strix come from, Duat, and the underworld of the Helmenth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T03:37:45-07:00","id":146554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=145499#post145499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage: Astral -&gt; Supernal<br /> Chengeling: Hedge -&gt; Arcadia<br /> Werewolf: Shadow -&gt; Penumbra</div> </div> </div> </div>I would glady hear were is Penumbra described in <b>Forsaken </b>gamline, as this <b>Apocalypse</b> &quot;deep spiritual dismension&quot; was a thing I missed to make <b>Werewolf </b>a more mature line... Or is this Anima Mundi from <b>Mage</b>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T05:02:08-07:00","id":146582,"title":"","content":"The term Penumbra isn't really used in Forsaken. Some books (of the Forsaken, Mage and bluebook lines) do imply there is a &quot;deep shadow&quot;, consisting of pocket realms that cannot be directly mapped to the real world. These realms are also the places where high rank incarna hold their court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T07:33:08-07:00","id":146718,"title":"","content":"The only true knowledge of the World of Darkness is that nobody knows nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T22:56:20-07:00","id":147634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=146582#post146582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term Penumbra isn't really used in Forsaken. Some books (of the Forsaken, Mage and bluebook lines) do imply there is a &quot;deep shadow&quot;, consisting of pocket realms that cannot be directly mapped to the real world. These realms are also the places where high rank incarna hold their court.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know a <b>Mage</b> line rather good, but don't remeber this tibits. Could you write were to find them in <b>Werewolf</b> or <b>Mage</b>, precisly?<br /> <br /> Also, as there was Idigam spoiler yasterday - are this &quot;Penumbra&quot; a Moon's/Luna's Realm also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T00:12:30-07:00","id":147688,"title":"","content":"I don't recall the word penumbra used at all, though if it's a mage term that might explain it.<br /> <br /> In the Werewolf the Forsaken Core and the Book of Spirits it calls them, 'Places-That-Aren't.' And they're mentioned a few times in Forsaken stuff. They're like the 13th floors of buildings and so forth. There's also mention of doors to 'strange places that seem to have no relationship to the world we know.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-24-2014, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T00:20:55-07:00","id":147690,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall so-called &quot;deep shadow&quot; which didn't really correspond to the current material realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T03:00:33-07:00","id":147753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=147634#post147634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know a <b>Mage</b> line rather good, but don't remeber this tibits. Could you write were to find them in <b>Werewolf</b> or <b>Mage</b>, precisly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nofather already pointed out the &quot;Places-That-Aren't&quot;, which is how they are called in the Book of Spirits and Forsaken. The main reference in Mage is in our favorite cosmology building book, Imperial Mysteries, on p. 64 under &quot;Gods of Shadow&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: &quot;Places-That-Aren't&quot; are on p. 74 of the Book of Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T06:23:57-07:00","id":147796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=147688#post147688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall the word penumbra used at all, though if it's a mage term that might explain it.<br /> <br /> In the Werewolf the Forsaken Core and the Book of Spirits it calls them, 'Places-That-Aren't.' And they're mentioned a few times in Forsaken stuff. They're like the 13th floors of buildings and so forth. There's also mention of doors to 'strange places that seem to have no relationship to the world we know.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits with Mass Create can presumably make those realms. So indeed, you could find the very Firstborn's Hunting Grounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T00:19:43-07:00","id":148454,"title":"","content":"It's weird they didn't get proper sourcebook yet. But I will surely use them as Firstborns &quot;homeworld&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:03:03-07:00","id":148730,"title":"","content":"Isn't the Mage cosmology the most unified cosmology? At least they the broadest view of all of the splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:14:35-07:00","id":148736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=148730#post148730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the Mage cosmology the most unified cosmology? At least they the broadest view of all of the splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even close.<br /> <br /> There's so much stuff out there that the mages don't even <i>account</i> for, let alone understand or work into their universal model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T10:25:39-07:00","id":154966,"title":"","content":"The game I am about to run is largely Masquerade run using NWOD mechanics, and the truth behind the universe is so incomprehensible to anything remotely human that you either cannot know it in full or have become something inhuman that can. I do however have a set of basic &quot;Laws&quot; that manage everything for consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3161-goliath","name":"Goliath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:09:12-07:00","id":155012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144922-unified-cosmology?p=148736#post148736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even close.<br /> <br /> There's so much stuff out there that the mages don't even <i>account</i> for, let alone understand or work into their universal model.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is you have Tier 4 entities constantly screwing with the map so even if you're map is 100% correct at this very second, the pieces will eventually start moving around. Some Archmage may find it funny to put merge the Hedge and Twilight and smack the realm of the True Fae up against the Shadow. Another may decided to throw merge the Inferno into the Underworld. <br /> <br /> The world is a pinball machine for these creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T06:39:47-07:00","id":1462124,"title":"","content":"This is my attempt to reconcile the Supernal Realms, the god-machine, emanation realms, the Lower Depths (still not totally happy with it) and Duat. None of the art, pictures, symbols (or otherwise) are my own creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/kxdoV7c\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/kxdoV7c\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/kxdoV7c\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/gallery/kxdoV7c </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26862-danieltallon","name":"Danieltallon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}